<title>HUNGARY: Hungary's May c/a surplus $148mln, trade gap $42mln.</title>
<headline>Hungary's May c/a surplus $148mln, trade gap $42mln.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary had a current account surplus of $148 million and a trade deficit of $42 million in May, according to preliminary figures from the National Bank of Hungary on Friday.</p>
<p>HUNGARY CURRENT ACCOUNT (in million dollars)</p>
<p>		   May 97  Apr 97   Jan-May 97  May 96  Jan-May 96</p>
<p> Trade balance   -42     -204	-648	-161     -934</p>
<p>  - Exports    1,561    1,779     7,829     1,232    5,618</p>
<p>  - Imports    1,603    1,983     8,477     1,393    6,552</p>
<p>Services and</p>
<p>    income	  99	  9	 -65	  76     -225</p>
<p>  - Tourism	136	123	 417	 115	309</p>
<p>- Capital</p>
<p>    investment   -37	-85	-448	 -61     -653</p>
<p>- Other</p>
<p>current</p>
<p>    payments	 1	-29	 -35	  22	119</p>
<p>Unrequited</p>
<p>    transfers     91	 84	 274	  95	421</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Current account 148     -110	-439	  10     -738</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Foreign direct capital</p>
<p>    investments  495	185     1,051	 131	645</p>
<p>NOTE - May 1997 figures are preliminary. Central bank trade figures are based on cash flow data, while Ministry of Industry, Trade and Tourism trade figures are based on customs statistics.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
